```
function findIndices($L, $T) {
  $H = array(); // initialize an empty hash table
  $n = count($L);
  for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
    $x = $L[$i];
    $complement = $T - $x;
    if (isset($H[$complement])) {
      return array($H[$complement], $i); // return the indices of the two integers
    }
    $H[$x] = $i; // add the current element to the hash table
  }
  return null; // if no pair is found, return null
}
```
This function takes in the list $L$ and the target sum $T$, and returns an array containing the indices of the two integers that add up to $T$, or null if no such pair exists. The time complexity of this algorithm is O(n), since we only iterate through the list once and each hash table lookup takes constant time on average.

