To ensure that the supervised and unsupervised components work effectively together, you can use a pre-training and fine-tuning approach. First, pre-train the unsupervised component using an unsupervised learning algorithm such as autoencoder or RBM. Then, fine-tune the entire network using supervised learning with the labeled data. This approach can help the network learn useful features from the unsupervised component that can improve the performance of the supervised component. 
