```java
import java.util.Scanner;
public class SentenceIdentifier {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter a sentence: ");
        String sentence = scanner.nextLine().trim();
        scanner.close();
        int numWords = sentence.split("\\s+").length;
        int numChars = sentence.replaceAll("\\s+", "").length();
        String sentenceType;
        char lastChar = sentence.charAt(sentence.length() - 1);
        switch (lastChar) {
            case '.':
                sentenceType = "declarative";
                break;
            case '?':
                sentenceType = "interrogative";
                break;
            case '!':
                sentenceType = "exclamatory";
                break;
            default:
                sentenceType = "imperative";
                break;
        }
        System.out.printf("%s sentence with %d words and %d characters", sentenceType, numWords, numChars);
    }
}
```
In this updated program, we first prompt the user to enter a sentence and then use `Scanner` to read the input. We then use the `trim()` method to remove any leading or trailing whitespace from the sentence.
