To get the number of characters in the sentence, we use the `replaceAll()` method to remove all whitespace characters from the sentence and then use the `length()` method to get the length of the resulting string.
We then use a `switch` statement to determine the type of the sentence based on the last character in the sentence. If the last character is a period, the sentence is declarative; if it is a question mark, the sentence is interrogative; if it is an exclamation mark, the sentence is exclamatory; otherwise, the sentence is imperative.
