Here is a recipe for a three-layered cake with alternating flavors and colors, with a distinct filling between each layer.
\section*{Ingredients}
\begin{itemize}
  \item 2 cups all-purpose flour
  \item 2 tsp baking powder
  \item 1/2 tsp salt
  \item 1/2 cup unsalted butter, softened
  \item 1 1/4 cups granulated sugar
  \item 2 large eggs
  \item 1 tsp vanilla extract
  \item 3/4 cup whole milk
  \item Food coloring (optional)
  \item 1 batch of your favorite frosting
  \item 1 batch of your favorite filling (e.g. fruit preserves, caramel sauce, etc.)
\end{itemize}
\section*{Kitchen Tools}
\begin{itemize}
  \item Three 8-inch cake pans
  \item Electric mixer
  \item Mixing bowls
  \item Rubber spatula
  \item Cooling rack
  \item Piping bag (optional)
\end{itemize}
\section*{Instructions}
\subsection*{Step 1: Preheat the Oven}
Preheat your oven to 350°F (180°C). Grease and flour three 8-inch cake pans.
\subsection*{Step 2: Make the Batter}
In a medium bowl, whisk together the flour, baking powder, and salt. In a separate large bowl, cream the butter and sugar together until light and fluffy. Beat in the eggs, one at a time, followed by the vanilla extract. Gradually add the dry ingredients to the wet ingredients, alternating with the milk, and mix until just combined.
If you want to create different colored layers, divide the batter into separate bowls and mix in food coloring until you achieve the desired color.
\subsection*{Step 3: Bake the Cake Layers}
Pour the batter into the prepared cake pans, making sure to spread it evenly. Bake for 20-25 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted into the center of each cake comes out clean. Remove the cakes from the oven and let them cool on a wire rack for 10 minutes before removing them from the pans.
\subsection*{Step 4: Assemble the Cake}
Once the cake layers are completely cooled, it's time to assemble the cake. Place one cake layer on a serving plate or cake stand. Spread a layer of filling (e.g. fruit preserves, caramel sauce, etc.) on top of the first cake layer. Add the second cake layer on top of the filling and repeat the process. Finally, add the third cake layer on top of the second layer and spread a thin layer of frosting over the entire cake to create a "crumb coat." This will help the final layer of frosting to stick better.
Refrigerate the cake for 30 minutes to allow the crumb coat to set. Then, add a final layer of frosting to the cake. You can use a piping bag to create decorative designs on the cake, if desired.
\subsection*{Step 5: Serve and Enjoy!}
Slice the cake and serve immediately. Store any leftover cake in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to three days.
The ideal temperature and baking time for each layer will depend on your oven and the thickness of the cake layers. Generally, baking at 350°F (180°C) for 20-25 minutes should give you a good result. However, you may need to adjust the temperature and baking time slightly based on your specific recipe and oven.

