First, we need to calculate the distance rate: 
\begin{equation}
Distance \cdot Rate = 800 \cdot 0.50 = 400
\end{equation}
Next, we add the additional fees: 
\begin{equation}
400 + 5 = 405
\end{equation}
Then, we calculate the taxes: 
\begin{equation}
Taxes = 0.08 \cdot 405 = 32.40
\end{equation}
Finally, we add the taxes to the previous result to get the final shipping cost: 
\begin{equation}
Shipping Cost = 405 + 32.40 = 437.40
\end{equation}
Therefore, the shipping cost for a 10-pound package traveling from New York City to Chicago is $437.40.

